<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 38,194 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 38,194 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-10-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 38,194 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hpurs to 7 a.m. (0200 gmt) on Sunday, compared to 112,271 tonnes in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>    Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Sunday	   Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			 9,585	   12,703</p>
<p>    Import cargo			28,609	   99,568</p>
<p>    In the past 24 hours, five ships sailed and four berthed. In the next 24 hours three shipd were expected to sail and seven were expected to arrive.</p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		  Berthing</p>
<p>Sugar		    12,500	 Arad		 10/10</p>
<p>Palm oil		 16,000	 Bunga Sepang     15/10</p>
<p>High speed deisel    26,000	 Sand Gate	  12/10</p>
<p>Crude oil		65,000	 Capitan Mirinda  13/10</p>
<p>Sugar		    14,000	 Azovlloyed	   due</p>
<p>Sugar		    12,500	 Amer Prabha	  due</p>
<p>Feul oil		 42,000	 Probo Hawk	   due</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
